# Initial Setup's Advanced page, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigAdvanced.cs.
#
# InitialSetup adds it in the Advanced view whether or not a vehicle is connected, as the heading
# of Terminal and Script REPL (InitialSetup.cs:340-353); choosing it shows the page and opens the
# heading. Its Activate does nothing and it reads no parameter, so this script runs with no link:
# the data directory is a scratch one, so no link Mission Planner remembers is opened. It needs
# no SITL, and there is no parameter on the page to write.
#
# The claims: the page shows label1's text and the table's thirteen buttons with the label beside
# each, in the .resx's order, and every button is dimmed - each opens a window of its own
# (ConfigAdvanced.cs:22-127: the Warnings Manager, MAVLink Inspector, proximity, signing keys,
# MAVLink mirror, NMEA output, Follow Me, parameter regeneration, moving base, log anonymiser, FFT,
# spectrogram, support proxy) that this application does not have. The script clicks none of
# them; config/advanced.rs's tests hold the controls to the Designer and the .resx and each
# handler to the window its row names.

env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK

screen setup
window 1600x1200
settle 3

expect config.advanced.active false
expect setup.pages ~ ConfigAdvanced,ConfigTerminal
click setup-page-ConfigAdvanced
settle 1
expect setup.page ConfigAdvanced
expect setup.title Advanced
expect setup.expanded ConfigAdvanced
expect setup.shown ConfigFirmwareManifest,ConfigFirmware,ConfigSecureAP,ConfigOptional,ConfigAdvanced,ConfigTerminal
expect config.advanced.active true
expect config.advanced.text The following pages are for advanced configutation only. use with caution
expect config.advanced.buttons Warning Manager,MAVLink Inspector,Proximity,Mavlink Signing,Mavlink Mirror,NMEA,Follow Me,Param gen,Moving Base,Anon Log,FFT,Spectrogram,Support Proxy
expect config.advanced.labels ~ Enable custom warnings based on a set of conditions|View decoded mavlink data
expect config.advanced.labels ~ |Share connection with support engineer
expect config.advanced.buttons.enabled false
expect config.advanced.dimmed ~ but_mavinspector: the MAVLink Inspector window (Controls/MAVLinkInspector.cs) is not ported

# The heading again closes it, and Advanced is still the page showing; another page and it is not.
click setup-page-ConfigAdvanced
settle 1
expect setup.page ConfigAdvanced
expect setup.shown ConfigFirmwareManifest,ConfigFirmware,ConfigSecureAP,ConfigOptional,ConfigAdvanced
expect config.advanced.active true
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
settle 1
expect setup.page ConfigOptional
expect config.advanced.active false
